<h1>GitHub pull requests</h1>
<p class="hint">
  Compare GitHub's text diff with a semantic view of changed UnityYAML assets. The sample pull request below uses
  fixture files and the extension's WebAssembly diff engine; it does not connect to GitHub.
</p>

<div class="window">
  <div class="window-title">github.com/you/unity-project/pull/1/files</div>
  <div class="gh-page">
    <h1 class="pr-header">Rebalance robot physics and rework the playground scene <span class="pr-number">#1</span></h1>
    <p class="pr-meta">
      {{ pullRequest.files.size }} files changed between <span class="branch">{{ pullRequest.base }}</span> and
      <span class="branch">{{ pullRequest.head }}</span>
    </p>
    {% for file in pullRequest.files %}
      {% include 'file-card.liquid', file: file %}
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</div>
<script src="demo.js" defer></script>

<h2>Try the demo</h2>
<p>Use the PrefabLens switch above the changed files, or the switch beside a file, to move between <strong>Raw</strong> and <strong>Semantic</strong> views. The sample data is bundled with this page, so the demo does not need GitHub sign-in.</p>

<h2>Use PrefabLens on GitHub</h2>
<p><a href="https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/dlhnalbfkikchkfedfneiimadommcnip">Install PrefabLens from the Chrome Web Store</a>, then open the <strong>Files changed</strong> tab of a pull request. Select <strong>Semantic</strong>. If asked, sign in through GitHub Device Flow to load the pull request's file contents.</p>
<p>The extension requests file contents and pull request metadata from GitHub. Read the <a href="https://github.com/hashiiiii/PrefabLens/blob/main/PRIVACY.md">privacy policy</a> and the <a href="https://github.com/hashiiiii/PrefabLens/blob/main/docs/extension.md">extension guide</a>.</p>
